5. Update `index.md` â€” add a new entry with link, one-line summary, category, date.
6. Update every existing wiki page the new source touches. A single SOP can update 10â€“15 pages: concept pages get new examples, playbooks get new steps, the Marcus page gets new pain points, the glossary gets new terms.
7. Use `[[wiki-link]]` syntax for every reference to another wiki page so Obsidian's graph view stays useful.
8. If new data contradicts an existing claim in the wiki, do NOT silently overwrite. Flag it inline: `> âš ï¸ Contradiction: this contradicts [[older-page]] which claimed X. Resolution: ...`
9. Append an entry to `log.md`.
10. Show the user every file touched.

